   "evidence": "The proof uses `Units.smul_def` only to turn unit actions into scalar actions; `smul_smul`, `map_smul` and `cycleCoeff_succ` do not need invertibility, and `cycleCoeff` is defined for `[CommMonoid M]`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/WeightedCycle/Family/SignedPerm.lean",
   "fix": "State it as `pow_apply_of_apply_eq_smul (s : \u03b9 \u2192 R) (h : \u2200 i, f (v i) = s i \u2022 v (\u03c0 i)) : (f ^ r) (v x) = \u03c0.cycleCoeff s x r \u2022 v ((\u03c0 ^ r) x)`. Derive the `\u2124\u02e3` use in `Matrix.ShellLieAlgebra.reindex_pow_root` by coercing the weights and applying `Units.coe_prod`.",
   "issue": "`pow_apply_of_apply_eq_units_smul` requires `s : \u03b9 \u2192 R\u02e3`, but the induction never uses invertibility. For any weights `s : \u03b9 \u2192 R`, `f (v i) = s i \u2022 v (\u03c0 i)` implies `(f ^ r) (v x) = \u03c0.cycleCoeff s x r \u2022 v ((\u03c0 ^ r) x)`, because `Equiv.Perm.cycleCoeff` already works in any `CommMonoid`.",
   "line": 133
  }
